 (filename1 filename2 hash1 hash2)←{x}CompareVersions y;folder;filename;extension;tempFolder;rc;msg;data;buff;hashes;path1;path2
⍝ Extracts two versions of an APL object (or a file) from two commits and writes them to two
⍝ temporary files, ready to be compared.\\
⍝ `y` is either just `name` or `(name hash1)` or `(name hash1 hash2)`:
⍝ * `name` may be an APL object or a filename; for the details see `IdentifyObject`.
⍝ * Without any hashes the two most recent commits that changed the object are taken.
⍝ * With just one hash that one is compared with the most recent commit.\\
⍝ For what `x` can actually be see `EstablishProject`.\\
⍝ Returns the two filenames together with the two hashes they stem from, or four empty vectors
⍝ in case there are not enough commits to compare.\\
⍝ The two files are the only inhabitants of a temporary folder of their own, so a caller may
⍝ remove that folder - `⊃⎕NPARTS filename1` - once she is done with them.\\
⍝ The file may have been renamed in the meantime: each version is taken from the path the file
⍝ had in that very commit; see `U.GetPathsInCommits`.\\
⍝ Note that this function never asks the user anything: when it needs to establish the hashes
⍝ itself it just takes the two most recent ones.
 x←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ ''}'x'
 filename1←filename2←hash1←hash2←''
 y←⊆y
 (filename folder)←x IdentifyObject⊃y
 hashes←1↓y
 :Select ≢hashes
 :Case 0
     →(2>≢buff←folder ChangeLog'./',filename)/0
     (hash1 hash2)←buff[1 2;1]
 :Case 1
     →(0=≢buff←folder ChangeLog'./',filename)/0
     hash1←⊃hashes
     hash2←(⊂1 1)⊃buff
 :Else
     (hash1 hash2)←2↑hashes
 :EndSelect
 (hash1 hash2)←{⍵↑⍨¨8⌊≢¨⍵}hash1 hash2              ⍝ Short version suffices
 'The two hashes match - that makes no sense'U.Assert hash1≢hash2
 extension←3⊃⎕NPARTS filename
 tempFolder←F.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-CompareVersions'
 (filename1 filename2)←tempFolder∘{⍺,'/',⍵}¨hash1 hash2,¨⊂extension
 (path1 path2)←folder U.GetPathsInCommits filename(hash1 hash2)
 (rc msg data)←folder U.RunGitCommand'show ',hash1,':',path1
 msg U.Assert 0=rc
 (⊂data)⎕NPUT filename1 1
 (rc msg data)←folder U.RunGitCommand'show ',hash2,':',path2
 msg U.Assert 0=rc
 (⊂data)⎕NPUT filename2 1
⍝Done
